n embedding converts data into numerical vectors representing semantic meaning.

For example:

"Dog"

might become:

[0.21, -0.34, 0.78, ...]

A sentence becomes a high-dimensional vector.

Why embeddings?

Consider:

"How can I reset my password?"

and

"I forgot my login password."

Different words, similar meaning.

Embeddings can represent them as vectors that are close together.

Semantic similarity
Dog       → [0.2, 0.4, 0.7]
Puppy     → [0.2, 0.5, 0.6]
Car       → [0.9, 0.1, 0.2]

Dog and Puppy are closer.
